        "id": 1
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T01:18:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you\u0027re right, and I think this is why we used to have  self._dispatcher_wake_event.wait(delay or 10) -- that means every 10 seconds at least we would re-evaluate the peek queue.\n\nI think we should put it back, but do so in a way where it\u0027s clear where that constant is coming from and why.  Something like adding:\n\n```\nPeekQueue.timeout \u003d 10\nGerritEventConnector.event_processing_interval \u003d PeekQueue.timeout\n```\n\nAnd then in the connection base class, change that line to  self._dispatcher_wake_event.wait(delay or self.event_processing_interval).\n\nThe other drivers with no PeekQueue can have event_processing_interval \u003d None.",
      "parentUuid": "1faa64ca_1cf7438f",
      "revId": "34c0a5d5004ec18fda25e17cea3fb1124e07a808",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
